<section class="paper">
  <div class="wrap story">
    <div class="side rv">
      <span class="k mono">\ My part</span>
      <h2>I direct it, shoot it, and <span class="serif">cut it.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="body rv">
      <p>I direct, shoot, and cut the Let's Get Started program spots, working alongside the agency Against and producer Tess Rizvi, with Vision Kit on stills. Every quarter we make four to six new films with a crew of five to twenty, and I build each one around the specific program, digging into what that path actually gives a student.</p>
      <p>Real students play the leads. On shoot days I run the set: directing the talent, shooting it, and keeping the crew moving with Tess on production, then I take it into the edit and cut it for every screen. I frame the students as the heroes and put the real tools and payoff of the program on screen.</p>
      <p>I've worked in Idaho education for more than ten years, and I bring that to every round. This one is homegrown, made with hometown friends and a client as fired up about it as I am. Together we're putting Idaho opportunities in front of the students who benefit most, and shifting the culture a little each quarter.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap catalog">
    <div class="cat-head rv">
      <span class="k mono">\ The scale</span>
      <h2>A quarterly machine, four years <span class="serif">deep.</span></h2>
      <p>Four to six new films every quarter, each one directed and shot from scratch, then cut down into every aspect ratio and run on TV and across social. Rounds one through six and counting.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cat-grid rv">
      {programs.map((p) => (<span class="cat-chip">{p.t}</span>))}
      <span class="cat-chip cat-more">+ more each quarter</span>
    </div>
    <p class="cat-note mono rv">On TV and social &nbsp;·&nbsp; every aspect ratio &nbsp;·&nbsp; :15 and :30 &nbsp;·&nbsp; four years and counting</p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap story">
    <div class="side rv">
      <span class="k mono">\ The results</span>
      <h2>The college keeps <span class="serif">climbing.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="body rv">
      <p>The real competitor was never other colleges. It was self-doubt. So the work skips the college-ad playbook, no campus tours, no logo-first branding, just the decision to start.</p>
      <!-- CWI's OWN enrollment figures (Idaho State Board of Education / Idaho Ed News, 2025).
           Context for the college the work serves, not claimed as a result of these films.
           Verified sources: tools/cwi-stats-verified.md -->
      <p>And the college it serves keeps growing. CWI has now posted <b>nine straight semesters</b> of enrollment growth, up <b>6.8%</b> last fall to more than <b>31,000</b> students, the largest community college in Idaho.</p>
      <p><b>98%</b> of CWI's students are Idahoans. Every one of those enrollments is a bet on the state, which is exactly why this work matters to me.</p>
      <p class="src mono">Enrollment: Idaho State Board of Education · Idaho Education News, 2025</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

